 "notes": [
  "Pilpel perfect Eccl.10.10 (קִלְקַל, \"[if the axe] is not sharpened\") was a previously-missing stem, plain non-ketiv tags -- an oversight unrelated to the recent ketiv-extraction fix. The identical inflected form (perfect 3ms, no prefix/suffix) also occurs at Ezek.21.26 (קִלְקַל בַּחִצִּים, \"he shook the arrows [for divination]\") -- a related but distinct sense of the same pilpel form; both share one stored slot per the dataset's one-citation-per-code convention, so the gloss covers both attested senses (\"sharpen\" and \"shake, brandish\") rather than picking one."
 ],
